			<div class="content" id="post-content-1717446">
									

<p>That is an impressively creepy picture. Unsubtle, but creepy.</p>
<p>It's good that this doesn't actually harm people; if it did, I would probably have downvoted. The note is quite good, although it got me envisioning the thing in the picture parading around carrying ads. Which is a pretty funny mental image.</p>
<p>This line in the containment procedures:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Suspected devices are to be targeted using self-uploading malware in order to disable the device until it can be seized by field agents.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Makes absolutely zero sense. It would make far more sense for the Foundation to just ask the major app marketplace runners (Google, Apple, etc.) to block this app, rather than adopt a more reactive approach.</p>

